  "id": "deduction",
  "term": "deduction",
  "definition": "Deduction is a form of indirect reasoning in which the conclusion is presented as necessarily following from the given propositions when their meaning and connection are understood. The term may refer to the mental process of working out that result, the relation between the starting points and the conclusion, or the conclusion itself.",
